{"id":"tq_0490","question":"What are two things you cannot eat for dinner?","answer":"Breakfast and lunch","answer_note":"Breakfast and lunch are meals that happen before dinner. By definition they cannot be eaten at dinner.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"The definition is the answer..."},
{"id":"tq_0491","question":"Why do the French eat snails?","answer":"Because they don't like fast food","answer_note":"A joke-style riddle: snails are notoriously slow, making them the opposite of 'fast food.'","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Culinary wordplay..."},
{"id":"tq_0492","question":"What time is it when the clock strikes 13?","answer":"Time to get a new clock","answer_note":"Clocks only go up to 12 — a clock striking 13 must be broken and needs replacement.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"One number too many..."},
{"id":"tq_0493","question":"What flies without wings, stings without a bee, and falls without legs?","answer":"Rain (flies = falls, stings = cold/pain, falls without legs = obvious)","answer_note":"Heavy rain falls from the sky, can sting the skin, and has no wings or legs.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Weather described in impossible terms..."},
{"id":"tq_0494","question":"If you have 3 oranges in one hand and 4 in the other, what do you have?","answer":"Very large hands","answer_note":"Holding 3 or 4 oranges in a single hand is physically difficult — the implied punchline is the size of the hands required.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Think about the hands, not the fruit..."},
{"id":"tq_0495","question":"What is always before you but can't be seen?","answer":"Your future","answer_note":"The future is always ahead of you in time but cannot be directly observed.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Invisible and inevitable..."},
{"id":"tq_0496","question":"I'm full of holes but can still hold a lot of water. What am I?","answer":"A sponge","answer_note":"Sponges are porous (full of holes) but absorb and hold water effectively.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Holes and water coexist here..."},
{"id":"tq_0497","question":"What number is odd but becomes even when you remove a letter?","answer":"Seven — remove the S to get 'even'","answer_note":"The number seven is odd (not divisible by 2). Remove the 'S' and you have 'even.'","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Letters turn odd into even..."},
{"id":"tq_0498","question":"What belongs to you but is used by everyone else more than you?","answer":"Your name","answer_note":"People say and use your name far more frequently than you say it yourself.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"easy","hook":"The most personal word, used by strangers..."},
{"id":"tq_0499","question":"A man is 6 feet tall, works as a butcher, wears size 11 shoes. What does he weigh?","answer":"Meat","answer_note":"A butcher weighs (measures) meat — that's literally what butchers do.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"His job is hidden in the question..."},
{"id":"tq_0500","question":"If you count 20 crows on a wire and a farmer shoots one, how many are left?","answer":"None — the shot scared the rest away","answer_note":"The gunshot would startle all remaining crows and they would fly away immediately.","category":"lateral thinking","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Sound has consequences..."},
{"id":"tq_0501","question":"What do you call a boomerang that won't come back?","answer":"A stick","answer_note":"A boomerang that doesn't return is just a stick — it has lost its defining characteristic.","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Function defines identity..."},
{"id":"tq_0502","question":"What is always the last thing to go to bed at night?","answer":"Your feet","answer_note":"When you get into bed, your feet are the last part of you to leave the floor and go into the bed.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Anatomy of getting into bed..."},
{"id":"tq_0503","question":"What's greater than God, more evil than the devil, the poor have it, the rich need it, and if you eat it you'll die?","answer":"Nothing","answer_note":"Nothing is greater than God, nothing is more evil than the devil, the poor have nothing, the rich need nothing, and eating nothing will kill you.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Every clue points to the same absence..."},
{"id":"tq_0504","question":"What is at the beginning of the end, and at the end of time and space?","answer":"The letter E","answer_note":"'End' starts with E, 'time' ends with E, 'space' ends with E.","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Letters hidden at every boundary..."},
{"id":"tq_0505","question":"What loses its head every time it bites?","answer":"A match","answer_note":"A match 'bites' (ignites) and loses its phosphorus head each time it strikes and burns.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Self-destructive by design..."},
{"id":"tq_0506","question":"What is the hardest key to turn?","answer":"A don-key (donkey)","answer_note":"A donkey contains 'key' but is notoriously stubborn and hard to turn.","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"easy","hook":"The animal hiding in the key..."},
{"id":"tq_0507","question":"I have no wings, but I can fly. I have no eyes, but I can cry. What am I?","answer":"A cloud","answer_note":"Clouds drift through the air (fly) and produce rain (cry) without wings or eyes.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"easy","hook":"The sky's most emotional traveler..."},
{"id":"tq_0508","question":"What kind of shoes can you make from banana skins?","answer":"Slippers","answer_note":"Banana skins cause slipping — making 'slippers' is the punny answer.","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Footwear from fruit..."},
{"id":"tq_0509","question":"You're running a race and pass the person in 2nd place. What place are you in now?","answer":"2nd place","answer_note":"Passing the 2nd place runner puts you in their position — 2nd place.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"You took their spot, not theirs and 1st..."},
{"id":"tq_0510","question":"How can you add 8 eights to get 1000?","answer":"888 + 88 + 8 + 8 + 8 = 1000","answer_note":"Using five 8s and three 8s (in the larger numbers): 888 + 88 + 8 + 8 + 8 = 1000.","category":"math tricks","difficulty":"hard","hook":"Eights arranged just right..."},
{"id":"tq_0511","question":"What has a mouth but cannot eat?","answer":"A river or a jar","answer_note":"Rivers have mouths (where they meet the sea) and jars have mouths (openings), but neither eats.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Anatomy in unexpected places..."},
{"id":"tq_0512","question":"What question can you never honestly answer 'no' to?","answer":"'Are you alive?' or 'Are you awake?'","answer_note":"If you can answer at all, you're alive and awake — saying 'no' would be self-defeating.","category":"logic","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Existence answers its own question..."},
{"id":"tq_0513","question":"What has only two words but thousands of letters?","answer":"A post office","answer_note":"'Post office' is two words but a post office contains thousands of letters (mail).","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Letters in the linguistic and postal sense..."},
{"id":"tq_0514","question":"A man is pushing his car and stops at a hotel. He says he's bankrupt. What game is he playing?","answer":"Monopoly","answer_note":"In Monopoly, you push your car token and landing on a hotel property can bankrupt you.","category":"lateral thinking","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Life-size board game..."},
{"id":"tq_0515","question":"I have many teeth but I cannot bite. What am I?","answer":"A comb","answer_note":"A comb has many teeth (the prongs) but cannot bite like an animal.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Toothful but harmless..."},
{"id":"tq_0516","question":"What is the fastest thing in the universe?","answer":"Light (approximately 299,792,458 m/s in a vacuum)","answer_note":"Light travels at approximately 300,000 km/s — the ultimate cosmic speed limit according to relativity.","category":"science tricks","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Nothing catches what nothing can stop..."},
{"id":"tq_0517","question":"What can you swallow that can also swallow you?","answer":"Water","answer_note":"You swallow water to drink, but water (as in a flood, ocean, or drowning) can swallow you.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"medium","hook":"A reversible relationship..."},
{"id":"tq_0518","question":"What is the most common four-letter word used in English?","answer":"'That' or 'with' or 'have'","answer_note":"'That' consistently ranks as one of the most common four-letter words in English text.","category":"language","difficulty":"medium","hook":"The most used word most people can't name..."},
{"id":"tq_0519","question":"What do you get when you cross a snowman and a vampire?","answer":"Frostbite","answer_note":"Frost (from snowman) + bite (from vampire) = frostbite. A cold-weather hazard and a pun.","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Monster math..."},
{"id":"tq_0520","question":"What is a word made up of 4 letters, yet is also made up of 3. Sometimes is written with 9 letters. What is it?","answer":"The answer IS the question — 'what' has 4 letters, 'yet' has 3, 'sometimes' has 9","answer_note":"The riddle describes itself: 'What' (4), 'yet'/'and' (3), 'sometimes' (9).","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"hard","hook":"The riddle is its own answer..."},
{"id":"tq_0521","question":"How can you make the following equation true by adding one line: 5+5+5=550?","answer":"Make the first '+' into a 4: 545+5=550","answer_note":"Draw a horizontal line through the first + sign, turning it into a 4. This gives 545 + 5 = 550, which is true.","category":"math tricks","difficulty":"hard","hook":"One line changes everything..."},
{"id":"tq_0522","question":"What is always hungry and must be fed, and whatever it touches turns red?","answer":"Fire","answer_note":"Fire consumes fuel (always hungry, must be fed) and causes redness wherever it touches.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"easy","hook":"The consuming force..."},
{"id":"tq_0523","question":"What three numbers give the same result whether added or multiplied?","answer":"1, 2, and 3 (1+2+3=6 and 1×2×3=6)","answer_note":"1 + 2 + 3 = 6 and 1 × 2 × 3 = 6. The same result by both operations.","category":"math tricks","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Addition equals multiplication — when?"},
{"id":"tq_0524","question":"What has a bottom at the top?","answer":"Your legs","answer_note":"Your 'bottom' (backside) is located at the top of your legs.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Anatomy can be confusing..."},
{"id":"tq_0525","question":"How do you make number one disappear by adding a letter?","answer":"Add G before it: 'Gone'","answer_note":"G + one = gone. The number one is literally gone.","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"easy","hook":"A letter erases a number..."},
{"id":"tq_0526","question":"If I have 5 fish and 3 drown, how many do I have?","answer":"5 — fish don't drown","answer_note":"Fish breathe underwater through gills. They cannot drown in water. All 5 fish are still alive.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Biology saves the fish..."},
{"id":"tq_0527","question":"I am a word. When you add a letter to me, I become shorter. What am I?","answer":"'Short' — add 'er' to make 'shorter'","answer_note":"Adding 'er' to 'short' creates 'shorter' — a word that literally means more short.","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"easy","hook":"The paradox of comparative adjectives..."},
{"id":"tq_0528","question":"What do you call a deer with no eyes?","answer":"No-eye deer (no idea)","answer_note":"'No eye deer' sounds like 'no idea' — a phonetic pun.","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Animal phonics..."},
{"id":"tq_0529","question":"A plane crashes between the US and Canada. Where are the survivors buried?","answer":"Nowhere — you don't bury survivors","answer_note":"Survivors are alive. Living people are not buried anywhere.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"The same old trick, different location..."},
{"id":"tq_0530","question":"What is something everyone has but can never share?","answer":"Your thoughts (or your death, or your birth)","answer_note":"Thoughts occur in your mind uniquely. You can describe them, but the actual experience cannot be shared.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"medium","hook":"The most personal thing that cannot be given away..."},
{"id":"tq_0531","question":"What do you call a magic dog?","answer":"A labracadabrador","answer_note":"Labrador + abracadabra = Labracadabrador. The magical dog breed.","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Canine conjuring..."},
{"id":"tq_0532","question":"I'm tall when I'm young and short when I'm old. What am I?","answer":"A candle","answer_note":"A candle starts tall and burns shorter as it ages, becoming very short before disappearing.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Age works in reverse for this one..."},
{"id":"tq_0533","question":"What can you put between 7 and 8 to make the result greater than 7 but less than 8?","answer":"A decimal point — 7.8","answer_note":"Placing a decimal point between 7 and 8 creates 7.8, which is between 7 and 8.","category":"math tricks","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Punctuation as mathematics..."},
{"id":"tq_0534","question":"What is the only sport where the defense has the ball?","answer":"American football (when kicking)","answer_note":"In sports like baseball, cricket, and lacrosse, the defense can also have possession — but in most contexts football's punting is the classic answer.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Who has the ball in your sport?"},
{"id":"tq_0535","question":"What do you answer even though it never asks you a question?","answer":"A doorbell or a phone","answer_note":"You 'answer' a doorbell or phone call even though neither actually asks you a question.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Answering without being asked..."},
{"id":"tq_0536","question":"How many sides does a bowl have?","answer":"Two — inside and outside","answer_note":"A bowl has an inside surface and an outside surface — two sides, not zero.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Sides in three dimensions..."},
{"id":"tq_0537","question":"What word is always pronounced wrong?","answer":"'Wrong'","answer_note":"The word 'wrong' is spelled w-r-o-n-g and pronounced correctly every time. The trick is in the interpretation of 'always pronounced wrong.'","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"easy","hook":"The self-referential trap..."},
{"id":"tq_0538","question":"How can you spell 80 in two letters?","answer":"A-T (eight-y = A-T)","answer_note":"'Eighty' can be abbreviated phonetically as 'AT' — eight = A, y = T.","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"hard","hook":"Phonetic spelling in two letters..."},
{"id":"tq_0539","question":"What is the longest sentence in the world?","answer":"Life imprisonment","answer_note":"A 'sentence' can mean a prison term. Life imprisonment is the longest legal sentence.","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Two meanings of one word..."},
{"id":"tq_0540","question":"You walk into a room with a match. There's a candle, an oil lamp, and a fireplace. Which do you light first?","answer":"The match","answer_note":"You must light the match before anything else.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Always start with the source of fire..."},
{"id":"tq_0541","question":"What goes up but never comes down?","answer":"Your age","answer_note":"Age increases continuously and cannot decrease.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"easy","hook":"The one-directional number we all carry..."},
{"id":"tq_0542","question":"What animal can jump higher than a house?","answer":"Any animal — houses can't jump","answer_note":"A house is an inanimate structure. It cannot jump at all. Any jumping animal clears a house's jump height (zero).","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"The comparison is with a stationary object..."},
{"id":"tq_0543","question":"What did the ocean say to the beach?","answer":"Nothing — it just waved","answer_note":"Ocean waves are called 'waves' — the ocean 'waved' at the beach without saying a word.","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"easy","hook":"The ocean's silent greeting..."},
{"id":"tq_0544","question":"What has a lot of keys but can't open any door?","answer":"A piano or a keyboard","answer_note":"Pianos and keyboards have many keys but none of them unlock doors.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Keys that make music, not openings..."},
{"id":"tq_0545","question":"What 3-letter word completes all of these: _ss, _pp, _ff?","answer":"'A' — ass, app, aff — no. Better: 'O' — oss, opp, off","answer_note":"'O' completes: 'toss' (t+oss), 'topp'... Better answer: 'A' before all: 'ass, app, aff'. The puzzle requires letter patterns.","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"hard","hook":"Three letters completing three words..."},
{"id":"tq_0546","question":"What English word has the most definitions?","answer":"'Set' — over 430 definitions in the Oxford English Dictionary","answer_note":"'Set' holds the record for most definitions in the Oxford English Dictionary with over 430 separate meanings.","category":"language","difficulty":"hard","hook":"One tiny word, more meanings than most dictionaries have entries..."},
{"id":"tq_0547","question":"How can you lift an elephant with one hand?","answer":"You can't — you'll never find a one-handed elephant","answer_note":"The premise is impossible — elephants have four legs, not hands, and a 'one-handed elephant' doesn't exist.","category":"trick questions","difficulty":"easy","hook":"The trick hides in the elephant's anatomy..."},
{"id":"tq_0548","question":"What kind of cup can't hold water?","answer":"A cupcake","answer_note":"A cupcake has 'cup' in its name but cannot hold any liquid.","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Cup in name only..."},
{"id":"tq_0549","question":"What question must you always answer 'yes' to?","answer":"'Are you alive?' or 'Are you awake?'","answer_note":"If you can answer at all, you're alive and awake. 'No' is impossible while you're answering.","category":"logic","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Existence answers itself..."},
{"id":"tq_0550","question":"What can you catch that you can't throw?","answer":"A cold (or a glimpse, or feelings)","answer_note":"You catch a cold (get sick) but cannot throw one. Similarly with feelings or glimpses.","category":"riddles","difficulty":"easy","hook":"A very common catch..."},
{"id":"tq_0551","question":"What has 6 faces and 21 dots?","answer":"A die (singular of dice)","answer_note":"A standard six-sided die has 6 faces and dots totaling 1+2+3+4+5+6 = 21.","category":"math tricks","difficulty":"medium","hook":"The math of every board game..."},
{"id":"tq_0552","question":"If everyone bought a white car, what would we have?","answer":"A white car nation (a white carnation — the flower)","answer_note":"'White car nation' sounds like 'white carnation' — a phonetic wordplay.","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"medium","hook":"Traffic meets botany..."},
{"id":"tq_0553","question":"I am an odd number. Take away a letter and I become even. What number am I?","answer":"Seven — take away the S to get 'even'","answer_note":"Remove the 'S' from 'seven' and you have 'even' — the word, not the number.","category":"wordplay","difficulty":"easy","hook":"Letters turn numbers into concepts..."},
